/*!
    \page qwe-releases.html

    \title Qt WebEngine and Qt Pdf Releases
    \brief Information about Qt WebEngine and Qt Pdf versioning and release schedules.

    The Qt WebEngine and Qt Pdf, henceforth called QWE consists of a handful
    of \l{All Modules}{modules} and tools released under a common version number.
    In the following, we explain the versioning scheme and the related compatibility
    promises.

    \section1 Versioning and Compatibility

    QWE like Qt uses \l{https://semver.org/}{semantic versioning}. For more details see
    \l{https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qt-releases.html}. Similarly QWE offers the same compatibility
    promises of source and backwards binary compatibility as Qt.

    The QWE versioning scheme consist of major version to match the major Qt version, it
    is compatible with, and a minor version that states the Chromium version the QWE codebase
    was originally based on.

    \section1 Release schedules

    \e{Major} releases of Qt happen rarely---Qt 4.0.0 was released in 2005, Qt 5.0.0
    in 2012, and Qt 6.0.0 in 2020.

    \e{Minor} releases of QWE happen two or three times a year.

    For each minor release, we typically provide a \e{patch} release every four weeks ---
    until the next minor release of QWE is out. With releases breaking schedule if new critical
    issues actively exploit are discovered.

*/
